  "title": "Barry Marshall: Why Did This Doctor Drink Bacteria?",
  "description": "Barry Marshall drank a glass of bacteria on purpose, and it changed how the world treats stomach ulcers.\n\nIn 1984, doctors blamed ulcers on stress and acid. In Perth, Australia, Marshall and pathologist Robin Warren kept finding a spiral bacterium, Helicobacter pylori, in sick stomachs, but nobody believed them. So Marshall drank a culture of it. Within days he was vomiting, and an endoscopy showed an inflamed stomach. In 2005, Marshall and Warren shared the Nobel Prize in Medicine, and today ulcers caused by this germ are treated with antibiotics.\n\nSubscribe to Stickstory for a new true story every day. Would you have drunk it to prove you were right? Tell me in the comments!\n\n#shorts #barrymarshall #hpylori #stickstory",
